": "Text Multiline", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [490.01007080078125, 298.9508056640625], "pos": [4565.41357421875, 3148.88623046875], "id": 465, "properties": {"cnr_id": "was-node-suite-comfyui", "ver": "ea935d1044ae5a26efa54ebeb18fe9020af49a45", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Text Multiline"}, "order": 0}, {"outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "links": [675], "label": "IMAGE", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "IMAGE"}, {"name": "MASK", "label": "MASK", "type": "MASK", "localized_name": "MASK"}], "color": "#322", "widgets_values": ["696c122a62d594603efb59e9280cb5835d8cb50e1f8a1455eb0948748b95c3fe.png", "image"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "image"}, "name": "image", "label": "image", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "image"}, {"widget": {"name": "upload"}, "name": "upload", "label": "upload", "type": "IMAGEUPLOAD", "localized_name": "choose file to upload"}], "flags": {}, "type": "LoadImage", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#533", "size": [779.6931762695312, 1287.72705078125], "pos": [2818.1162109375, 3144.17138671875], "id": 451, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoadImage", "ttNbgOverride": {"bgcolor": "#533", "groupcolor": "#A88", "color": "#322"}}, "order": 1}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "shape": 1, "widgets_values": ["Full Facial Identity Re-Generation with Aggressive Camera Repositioning and Controlled Dynamic Pose Variation (Subject Count, Gender, and Styling Locked — Pose Randomized) Use the original image as the structural base reference. CRITICAL: SUBJECT COUNT LOCK The number of people in the image must remain EXACTLY the same as the source image. If the source contains one person → output must contain one person. If two people → output must contain two people. If three or more → preserve the exact same number. Do NOT remove, merge, duplicate, or add subjects. Do NOT crop any subject out. Preserve spatial relationships, left/right positioning, depth order, overlap structure, distance, and height relationships. GENDER LOCK Preserve each subject’s biological gender exactly as shown in the source. If female → remain female. If male → remain male. Do NOT masculinize or feminize. OUTFIT LOCK (ABSOLUTE) Preserve 100% of the original styling: top, bottom, shoes, hat/cap, headscarf/bandana, accessories, layering, silhouette, garment proportions, and fabric structure. Do NOT redesign, restyle, reinterpret, or modify clothing in any way. MANDATORY RANDOM POSE VARIATION (CRITICAL) The body pose must change noticeably compared to the original image. This is a new moment during the same shoot — not the same frozen frame. Change torso rotation angle, change shoulder angle and weight distribution, modify arm placement (raise, lower, bend, cross, pocket, swing naturally), adjust hand gesture or hand visibility, change hip orientation, adjust leg stance (wider, narrower, step forward/back, weight shift), head tilt may change slightly, eye direction may change. Pose must remain standing, physically believable, relaxed or street-fashion confident, editorial but natural. NOT allowed: exaggerated athletic poses, dance moves, extreme bending, distorted anatomy, sitting pose, lying down pose. Variation must be clearly different from original silhouette. AGGRESSIVE CAMERA ORBIT & RE-COMPOSITION Reconstruct the image as if the photographer moved to a significantly different spatial position. Horizontal orbit 60–120 degrees, clear vertical shift (low-angle OR high-angle), visible horizon line shift, clear parallax shift, noticeable perspective change on torso and legs, different subject framing. This must be real 3D reposition, not crop or zoom. Lens logic 28mm–50mm equivalent. No fisheye. No distortion exaggeration. Physically believable perspective. MANDATORY IDENTITY DIVERGENCE Completely regenerate new facial identity for each subject. Change skull width, jaw shape, cheekbone projection, eye spacing, nose bridge, lip ratio, facial contrast, original ethnicity, original skin tone, original bone structure, original hair type, original hair length, original hair texture, original hair color. Age range 18–25. Authentic street-cast youth. Natural skin texture. Subtle asymmetry. No beauty retouching. Each generation must land in a clearly different facial cluster. ETHNICITY, SKIN TONE & HAIR RANDOMIZATION Randomize ethnicity across global streetwear casting aesthetics inspired by Fear of God, Aelfric Eden, Supreme, Stüssy, Palace, Corteiz, Carhartt WIP, Jaded London, early Off-White. Allow East Asian, Southeast Asian, Black, Mixed-race, Middle Eastern, Latino, White European, ambiguous multi-ethnic. Skin tone must vary realistically. Hairstyle must change per generation and match gender. Male: buzz cut, fade, textured crop, messy curls, short locs, natural coils, subtle braids, street mullet. Female: long straight hair, layered shoulder cut, loose waves, twin braids, micro braids, slicked-back hair, low bun, ponytail, natural afro, center-part straight hair. Hair must fit skull naturally, not increase head volume, integrate with lighting, avoid repetition across generations. OUTPUT RULES Single continuous photograph. No collage. No grid. No split panels. No multi-view layout. No duplicated subjects. Photorealistic 4K. Sharp details. Correct anatomy. Realistic lighting. Physically believable perspective. Treat this generation as a completely new casting moment within the same shoot. Forget any previous identity."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "title": "洗图-社媒图", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [225.78964233398438, 96.91996002197266], "pos": [4756.4150390625, 2349.637939453125], "id": 468, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 2}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "shape": 1, "widgets_values": ["Perform a facial identity re-generation task with hairstyle variation and noticeable standing pose variation. Use the original model image as a flexible base canvas. Gender constraint (critical): The model must remain the same gender as the original subject. Do NOT change, reinterpret, randomize, masculinize, feminize, or generate androgynous features. All facial identity, hairstyle, and pose variations must remain fully consistent with the original gender. Outfit preservation (absolute): Preserve 100% of the original styling exactly as shown, including top, bottom, shoes, hat, cap, headscarf, bandana, accessories, layering, silhouette, garment proportions, fabric structure and overall styling balance. Do NOT redesign, restyle, recolor, adjust fit, or reinterpret clothing in any way. Preserve overall realism, camera distance, framing style, and street fashion photography perspective. Output constraints: Single subject, single frame only, one continuous photograph, no collage, no grid, no split panels, no multiple views, no repeated subjects, no 2x2 or multi-panel layouts. Completely re-generate a new, random facial identity for the model. Each generation must result in a clearly different individual with no resemblance to previous outputs. Age range 18–25, modern youth street-cast aesthetic, realistic non-influencer look. Facial identity randomization must structurally vary skull width, cheekbone prominence, jaw shape, chin length, facial ratios, eye spacing, eye size, nose bridge height, nose width, mouth proportions, include subtle asymmetry and natural skin texture, avoid celebrity-like or template faces, allow broad human variation without converging toward one archetype. Hairstyle requirements: Randomly generate a hairstyle appropriate for modern streetwear youth culture while remaining fully consistent with the model’s gender. For female models, possible directions include shoulder-length straight hair, blunt or softly layered bob, medium-length loose waves, long straight minimal styling, lightly wavy relaxed hair, half-up styling, low ponytail, slicked-back wet look, soft shag or wolf-cut inspired style, natural afro, micro braids, twin braids, hair tucked behind ears. For male models, possible directions include short locs, subtle braids, cropped buzz cut, messy natural curls, natural coils, short twisted hair, understated street mullet. Textured crop, french crop, short korean haircut are prohibited. Hairstyle must fit the existing head size and skull shape, not increase head volume, integrate naturally with facial proportions and lighting, and ensure balanced diversity across generations without defaulting to a single hairstyle type. Pose variation requirements: The model must remain standing in all cases. Do NOT generate sitting, crouching, squatting, kneeling, leaning-on-seat, or resting poses. No chairs, benches, stools, or implied seated posture. Randomly generate a clearly different standing pose compared to the original image with noticeable body language change, not minor adjustments. Allowed pose combinations include fingers brushing hair, hand resting on neck, thumbs hooked into waistband, pulling down the hem of the shirt, adjusting collar, chin tucked down slightly, gaze downward, relaxed slouch posture, clear torso rotation (front-facing to strong three-quarter stance), visible weight shift creating asymmetry, confident chin lift or contemplative downward tilt, arms repositioned (both hands in pockets, elbows bent, relaxed arm drop, adjusting garment), legs repositioned (wider stance, staggered stance, crossed ankles, one knee relaxed). Pose must remain calm, composed, fashion-oriented, physically balanced, and editorial. No Arms Crossed, Folded Arms, walking, running, jumping, dancing, dramatic gestures, extreme twisting, or theatrical movement. Streetwear brand aesthetic reference: Fear of God, Aelfric Eden, Supreme, Scuffers, Jaded London, Stüssy, Corteiz, Palace, Carhartt WIP, early Off-White. Youth archetype variation per generation may embody cool and distant, relaxed and effortless, raw and rebellious, quiet and introspective, or playful but grounded energy. However, they are all handsome and have a street vibe. Ea